    "header": {
      "type": "page-header",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "About the College",
        "title": "",
        "text": "Formerly the College of Commerce, founded in 1935 at Central Philippine University in Jaro, Iloilo City."
      }
    },
    "intro": {
      "type": "split-feature",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Welcome",
        "heading": "Be a Centralian",
        "text": "<p>Welcome to Central Philippine University especially to the College of Business and Accountancy. You have made the right decision in choosing your degree. We are grateful that you are now a member of the CBA family. Continue to soar high and hit your goal. You would be one of these persons in the future: A Certified Public Accountant, Certified Management Accountant, Certified Bookkeeper, Cost Accountant, Comptroller, Finance Officer, Manager, VP Finance, President of the Company, CEO, Treasurer, Banker, Entrepreneur and many more.</p><p>There are lots more to equip yourself as a whole person in order to face the complexity and challenges in the business world. The curriculum was thoroughly designed for every program offered to cater the needs of students academically. Convocations during Christ Emphasis Week celebration would strengthen your faith in God and you would be spiritually filled and morally secured. The activities done by the student organizations will improve you socially.</p><p>Be a CENTRALIAN, let us work together for our success. Be determined, have faith in God and focus on achieving your goals.</p>",
        "image_asset": "cba-faculty.jpg",
        "image_label": "Wide shot of the CPU campus or New Valentine Hall",
        "image_first": false,
        "button": "",
        "link": "",
        "style": "cream"
      }
    },
    "dean": {
      "type": "dean-message",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Message from the Dean",
        "heading": "Welcome to the CBA family",
        "body": "<p>Thank you for enrolling in one of the programs at Central Philippine University under the College of Business and Accountancy. It is our desire to equip you with knowledge and skills you need to face the complex business world. We hope that your life here at CPU would be meaningful and joyful.</p><p>Student life is not easy. It is full of challenges which will make you a better person. Enjoy the facilities, programs, and wholesome activities provided by the University. Make new friends, join in the student organizations, and participate in programs organized by your organizations. These will develop your interpersonal skills in working along with other people as well as your leadership capability. You would be academically, socially and spiritually equipped before you earn your degree and leave CPU behind.</p><p>We have so many things to be proud of in our college. Both the Bachelor of Science in Business Administration (BSBA) and Bachelor of Science in Accountancy (BSA) programs have Level IV Re-accreditation Status granted by ACSCU-AAI. The BSBA program is a \"Center of Excellence\" grantee of CHED.</p><p>Let us work hand in hand towards our success and in everything we do, let it be for the glory of GOD.</p>",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/866472804_2535828700269181_5915019450480083639_n.jpg",
        "name": "Dr. Lorna T. Grande",
        "role": "Dean, College of Business and Accountancy"
      }
    },
